{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-categorical-laplace-transform-properties","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:categorical-laplace-transform-properties","kind":"remark","title":"Base-ring independence of the categorical Laplace transform","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-laplace"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-laplace","tags":["hopf-algebra","grouplike","monoidal-functor","laplace"],"text":"categorical-laplace-transform-properties.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:categorical-laplace-transform-properties\"></a><p>The transform <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}</code> applies over any base ring <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{H}_q</code> supports the grouplike. Evaluating the pairing against the archimedean realisation recovers the integral <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\int_0^\\infty e^{-st} f(t) dt</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-laplace-transform-properties.md","heading":"Remark","number":"3.20.6"}
